title SHA-3 preference seated; post-quantum Kumara proposed, one quantum premise corrected
prompt Keaton asked to prioritize SHA3 over SHA2 for TAME reasons, and — if Ed25519 only uses SHA2 — to seat a breach/debride choosing a quantum-resistant SHA3-512-compatible curve for Kumara even if it breaks OpenSSH compat, to prevent collision vulnerabilities in the agentic-HPC decade and assert-block anything less secure as a root-README user promise
think Agreed with the SHA-3 preference on structural grounds (sponge, no length-extension, distinct lineage) and seated it — with the honesty guardrail that SHA-2 is not broken (SHA-512 has no practical collision/preimage break; the breaks were SHA-1/MD5), so we frame SHA-3 as a stronger design preference, never as a fix to a vulnerability an auditor would flag as false.
think Corrected one premise honestly: no elliptic curve is quantum-resistant — Shor breaks the curve's discrete log regardless of which hash it uses, so a SHA3-512 curve is still quantum-vulnerable; and 512-bit hashes are already quantum-safe (Grover only halves strength → ~256-bit margin). The quantum threat is the curve, not the hash.
think The honest realization of the goal is a post-quantum signature, not a curve — and the conservative ones (SLH-DSA/SPHINCS+ with SHAKE-256) are hash-based, so prefer-SHA-3 and post-quantum-Kumara become the same decision. Laid out three options: A SLH-DSA (hash-based, most auditable), B ML-DSA/Dilithium (lattice, fast, SHAKE), C hybrid Ed25519+PQ.
obs Kept the Ed25519 parity work — it proves our Rye crypto correct and stays load-bearing as the classical half if we choose the hybrid. Named a no-gate near-term crux the loop can take now: SHA3-256/512 + SHAKE-256 in Rye, parity vs Zig std.crypto + NIST FIPS 202 KATs (Monocypher carries no SHA-3).
obs Choosing Kumara's signature algorithm is foundational and custody-adjacent, so it waits for Keaton's word (asked as a question) rather than the loop's guess; signing with the identity key stays the custody gate. The security-floor assert-block and root-README promise are proposed, to seat once the floor algorithm is parity-GREEN.
